Under Article 37 of Law 4002/2011, the licence holder must issue a "Programme Document" (Έντυπο Προγράμματος) for each gambling game, in printed or electronic form [1]. For each game form included in it, the document must state:

- the form of the game;
- whether it is individual or team-based;
- the percentage of winnings paid out (το αποδιδόμενο ποσοστό κέρδους);
- other useful information specified by the Gaming Conduct and Control Regulation [1].

The document must also be displayed prominently in shops and on the entry page of the games website, and otherwise made available to players by any suitable means [1].
